#. column 0: rift sailor
#. column 2: rift sailors
#. column 8: The rift sailor uses the light elastic webbing between its wings to catch the roiling winds of the Sea of Clouds and glide across the rifts.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on medium canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:5042:0:9"
msgid "Rift Sailor"
msgstr "Парусник разломов"

#. ja: サゴリーモンクフィッシュ
#. de: Sagolii-Anglerfisch
#. fr: poisson lanterne de Sagolii
#. column 2: Sagolii monkfish
#. column 8: When hunting, the Sagolii monkfish uses a method similar to its sea-bound cousin─attracting potential prey to its location with a glowing appendage situated directly above its gaping maw.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Sagolii Monkfish
msgctxt "Item:5043:0:0"
msgid "Sagolii monkfish"
msgstr "саголийский удильщик"

#. de: Sagolii-Anglerfische
#. fr: poissons lanterne de Sagolii
#. column 0: Sagolii monkfish
#. column 8: When hunting, the Sagolii monkfish uses a method similar to its sea-bound cousin─attracting potential prey to its location with a glowing appendage situated directly above its gaping maw.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Sagolii Monkfish
msgctxt "Item:5043:0:2"
msgid "Sagolii monkfish"
msgstr "саголийские удильщики"

#. ja: 大型砂海魚。砂上に疑似餌状の器官を出し、獲物を誘って捕食する<br>[魚拓額縁G3に設定可能]
#. de: Auf der Jagd benutzt der Sagolii-Anglerfisch eine ähnliche Methode wie sein Artgenosse aus der Tiefsee - er lockt seine Beute mit einem winzigen leuchtenden Anhängsel an seinem Kopf in seinen gewaltigen Schlund. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe L ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Ce grand poisson des sables utilise son appendice comme appât pour attirer les proies à la surface du sable.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de grande taille]
#. column 0: Sagolii monkfish
#. column 2: Sagolii monkfish
#. column 9: Sagolii Monkfish
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:5043:0:8"
msgid "When hunting, the Sagolii monkfish uses a method similar to its sea-bound cousin─attracting potential prey to its location with a glowing appendage situated directly above its gaping maw.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]"
msgstr "Охотясь, саголийский удильщик действует почти как его морской родич: приманивает добычу светящимся отростком над своей огромной пастью.<br><br>[Можно выставить в большой раме с ихтиограммой.]"

#. ja: サゴリーモンクフィッシュ
#. de: Sagolii-Anglerfisch
#. fr: Poisson lanterne de Sagolii
#. column 0: Sagolii monkfish
#. column 2: Sagolii monkfish
#. column 8: When hunting, the Sagolii monkfish uses a method similar to its sea-bound cousin─attracting potential prey to its location with a glowing appendage situated directly above its gaping maw.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:5043:0:9"
msgid "Sagolii Monkfish"
msgstr "Саголийский удильщик"

#. ja: ソーサーフィッシュ
#. de: Tellerfisch
#. fr: poisson soucoupe
#. column 2: saucerfish
#. column 8: Lacking feet or wings to propel itself from the ground, only death awaits the saucerfish that is foolish enough to leave the Sea of Clouds.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Saucerfish
msgctxt "Item:5044:0:0"
msgid "saucerfish"
msgstr "рыба-блюдце"

#. de: Tellerfische
#. fr: poissons soucoupe
#. column 0: saucerfish
#. column 8: Lacking feet or wings to propel itself from the ground, only death awaits the saucerfish that is foolish enough to leave the Sea of Clouds.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Saucerfish
msgctxt "Item:5044:0:2"
msgid "saucerfish"
msgstr "рыбы-блюдца"

#. ja: 扁平した皿のような形状の雲海魚<br>[魚拓額縁G3に設定可能]
#. de: Da der Tellerfisch keine Flügel hat, um sich erneut in die Luft zu schwingen, sind die törichten Exemplare, die dem Wolkenmeer die Rückenflosse kehren, dem Tod geweiht. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe L ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Cet organisme simple vivant en milieux nuageux est coiffé d'une ombrelle qui ressemble à une soucoupe.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de grande taille]
#. column 0: saucerfish
#. column 2: saucerfish
#. column 9: Saucerfish
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:5044:0:8"
msgid "Lacking feet or wings to propel itself from the ground, only death awaits the saucerfish that is foolish enough to leave the Sea of Clouds.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]"
msgstr "У рыбы-блюдца нет ни ног, ни крыльев, чтобы подняться с земли. Покинув Море облаков, эта глупышка обречена на смерть.<br><br>[Можно выставить в большой раме с ихтиограммой.]"

#. ja: ソーサーフィッシュ
#. de: Tellerfisch
#. fr: Poisson soucoupe
#. column 0: saucerfish
#. column 2: saucerfish
#. column 8: Lacking feet or wings to propel itself from the ground, only death awaits the saucerfish that is foolish enough to leave the Sea of Clouds.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
msgctxt "Item:5044:0:9"
msgid "Saucerfish"
msgstr "Рыба-блюдце"

#. ja: キャラバンイール
#. de: Karawanen-Aal
#. fr: anguille nomade
#. column 2: caravan eels
#. column 8: After maturing in the Grand Wake, caravan eels will form long lines in the sand and make their way back to the Sagolii Desert to spawn and die.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Caravan Eel
msgctxt "Item:5045:0:0"
msgid "caravan eel"
msgstr "караванный угорь"

#. de: Karawanen-Aale
#. fr: anguilles nomades
#. column 0: caravan eel
#. column 8: After maturing in the Grand Wake, caravan eels will form long lines in the sand and make their way back to the Sagolii Desert to spawn and die.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]
#. column 9: Caravan Eel
msgctxt "Item:5045:0:2"
msgid "caravan eels"
msgstr "караванные угри"

#. ja: グランドウェイクで育ち、サゴリー砂漠に遡上してくる細長い砂海魚<br>[魚拓額縁G3に設定可能]
#. de: Wenn sie ausgewachsen sind, formen diese Aale lange Karawanen im Sand, um zum Laichen und Sterben in die Sagolii-Wüste zurückzukehren. (Kann als Fischdruck in Rahmen der Größe L ausgestellt werden.)
#. fr: Naissant dans les Tertres stériles, ce poisson des sables se fraye un chemin vers le désert de Sagolii une fois adulte.<br>[Affichable dans un cadre à ichtyogramme de grande taille]
#. column 0: caravan eel
#. column 2: caravan eels
#. column 9: Caravan Eel
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Item:5045:0:8"
msgid "After maturing in the Grand Wake, caravan eels will form long lines in the sand and make their way back to the Sagolii Desert to spawn and die.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on large canvases.]"
msgstr "Выросши в Великом следе, караванные угри выстраиваются в длинные цепочки на песке и возвращаются в пустыню Саголии, чтобы отложить икру и умереть.<br><br>[Можно выставить в большой раме с ихтиограммой.]"

#. ja: キャラバンイール
